(n) {C2} {transport by air} = ​a part of an aircraft's wing that can be raised in order to interrupt the flow of air over it and so slow the aircraft's speed, {C2} {transport by car or lorry} = a raised part on a fast car that prevents it from being lifted off the road when travelling very fast, {C2} {difficulty and failure} = a person or thing that intends or is intended to stop somebody/something being successful, {C2} {film and theatre} = information that you are given about what is going to happen in a film/television series/etc. before it is shown to the public